WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:00.923
- I'll be the first to admit

00:00:00.923 --> 00:00:03.060
that sometimes litigation is bananas.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.130
And such was the case in the
Epic versus Apple litigation

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:07.580
that's going forward right now,

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:09.690
when the parties had to discuss

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.370
one of the "Fortnite" characters, Peely,

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:12.860
who happens to be a banana

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:14.600
and things got hilarious from there.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.257
A lawyer for Apple introduced the issue,

00:00:16.257 --> 00:00:18.440
"We have a large yellow
banana here in a tuxedo?"

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:19.273
and the witness replies,

00:00:19.273 --> 00:00:20.290
"Yes, that's Peely."

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:22.400
The Apple lawyer says, "We
thought it was better to go

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:23.800
with a suit instead of the naked banana

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.950
because we're in federal court right now."

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:27.707
And then the Epic lawyer chimes in,

00:00:27.707 --> 00:00:29.380
"There might've been an
implication that showing Peely

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:31.090
without a suit might've
been inappropriate.

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:32.280
Is there anything inappropriate

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:33.670
about Peely without clothes?"

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:37.060
To which witness replied,
"It's just a banana, ma'am."

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:39.330
Because sometimes it's just a banana.

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:41.250
Now I'm sure that this is
not the last we've heard

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:44.400
of this banana because this
case is surely to be appealed

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.153
unless it gets too slippery.

